  "id": "Compound::DB00674 - Gene::1141",
  "verbalization": "Galantamine, a cholinesterase inhibitor, is shown to interact with multiple proteins involved in acetylcholine signaling, specifically through binding to Chrng, Chrne, and Chrna5. These proteins are all implicated in the regulation of acetylcholine-activated cation-selective channels, which are critical for neuronal function. The evidence suggests that Galantamine may modulate these channels by binding to their respective subunits, thereby influencing the activity of the channel complex. This mechanism is supported by the observed participation of these proteins in the same functional pathway, indicating a potential role in the regulation of acetylcholine signaling. The integrated evidence suggests that Galantamine may exert its effects on Chrnb2 through a direct interaction with one of these proteins, potentially altering the channel's activity and contributing to its therapeutic effects. The relationship is further supported by the consistent involvement of these proteins in the same functional context, reinforcing the hypothesis that Galantamine's interaction with Chrnb2 is mediated through a shared pathway involving acetylcholine-activated cation-selective channels.",
